ggml / llama.cpp
----------------
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

Used in: crates/quant (a port of ggml's quantization and dequantization code),
crates/core/src/ggml_type.rs (the numbering and block geometry of the weight
types), and the codebook tables generated from ggml-common.h
(crates/cuda/kernels/gen_iq_tables.py, crates/quant/tools/gen_tables.py).
From its server (tools/server at commit d92ea9bb126ab957849dd0c0f1f881a64de7dc86):
the request member `return_progress`, the stream's `prompt_progress` and when
it is sent (server-task.cpp, server-context.cpp; in
crates/server/src/openai/reply.rs, crates/server/src/responses/reply.rs and
crates/runtime/src/conductor/progress.rs), and the layout of the timings in the
log (print_timings and print_timings_pp of server-context.cpp; in
crates/server/src/bridge.rs).

